{"id":"mahabharata-6-056","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":56,"title":"षट्पञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 56 · Fourth day: Arjuna against Bhishma","summary":{"en":"At dawn Arjuna advances, enraged, against Bhishma, Drona, Duryodhana and the other Kaurava kings. His chariot with Krishna as charioteer crushes the front line and he and Bhishma fight a marvellous duel.","kn":"ಉದಯದಲ್ಲಿ ಅರ್ಜುನ ಕೋಪದಿಂದ ಭೀಷ್ಮ, ದ್ರೋಣ, ದುರ್ಯೋಧನರೇ ಮೊದಲಾದ ಕೌರವ ರಾಜರ ಮೇಲೆ ನುಗ್ಗುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಸಾರಥಿಯಾಗಿರುವ ಅವನ ರಥ ಮುಂಭಾಗವನ್ನು ಜಜ್ಜುತ್ತದೆ; ಅವನೂ ಭೀಷ್ಮನೂ ಅದ್ಭುತ ದ್ವಂದ್ವಯುದ್ಧ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"भोर में अर्जुन क्रोध से भीष्म, द्रोण, दुर्योधन और अन्य कौरव राजाओं पर बढ़ते हैं। कृष्ण-सारथी का उनका रथ अग्रपंक्ति को कुचलता है और वे भीष्म के साथ अद्भुत द्वन्द्व करते हैं।","te":"ఉదయం అర్జునుడు కోపంతో భీష్ముడు, ద్రోణుడు, దుర్యోధనుడు మొదలైన కౌరవ రాజులపైకి దూసుకెళతాడు. కృష్ణుడు సారథిగా ఉన్న అతని రథం ముందు వరుసను నలిపేస్తుంది; అతను, భీష్ముడు అద్భుత ద్వంద్వ యుద్ధం చేస్తారు.","ta":"விடியலில் அர்ஜுனன் சினத்துடன் பீஷ்மர், த்ரோணர், துரியோதனன் முதலிய கௌரவ மன்னர்களை நோக்கிப் பாய்கிறான். கண்ணன் செலுத்தும் அவன் தேர் முன்னணியை நசுக்க, அவனும் பீஷ்மரும் அற்புதமான தனிப்போர் புரிகின்றனர்.","ml":"പുലർച്ചെ ക്രോധത്തോടെ അർജുനൻ ഭീഷ്മർ, ദ്രോണർ, ദുര്യോധനൻ, മറ്റ് കൗരവ രാജാക്കന്മാർ എന്നിവർക്കെതിരെ മുന്നേറുന്നു. കൃഷ്ണൻ സാരഥിയായ രഥം മുൻനിര തകർക്കുന്നു; അർജുനനും ഭീഷ്മരും അത്ഭുതകരമായ ദ്വന്ദ്വയുദ്ധം നടത്തുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.56; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"व्युष्टां निशां भारत भारताना-\nमनीकिनीनां प्रमुखे महात्मा ।\nययौ सपत्नान्प्रति जातकोपो\nवृतः समग्रेण बलेन भीष्मः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the night had passed, Bharata, the great-souled Bhishma, angry at his foes, went out at the head of the Bharata armies, surrounded by his whole force."}},{"n":2,"text":"तं द्रोणदुर्योधनबाह्लिकाश्च\nतथैव दुर्मर्षणचित्रसेनौ ।\nजयद्रथश्चातिबलो बलौघै-\nर्नृपास्तथान्येऽनुययुः समन्तात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona, Duryodhana, Bahlika, Durmarshana, Chitrasena, and the very mighty Jayadratha, with other kings and their masses of troops, followed him on every side."}},{"n":3,"text":"स तैर्महद्भिश्च महारथैश्च\nतेजस्विभिर्वीर्यवद्भिश्च राजन् ।\nरराज राजोत्तम राजमुख्यै-\nर्वृतः स देवैरिव वज्रपाणिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounded by those great chariot-warriors and bright, valiant kings, he shone, best of kings, like the wielder of the thunderbolt among the gods."}},{"n":4,"text":"तस्मिन्ननीकप्रमुखे विषक्ता\nदोधूयमानाश्च महापताकाः ।\nसुरक्तपीतासितपाण्डुराभा\nमहागजस्कन्धगता विरेजुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the head of that host the great banners, tossed about and fastened to the shoulders of huge elephants, shone in red, yellow, black and white."}},{"n":5,"text":"सा वाहिनी शांतनवेन राज्ञा\nमहारथैर्वारणवाजिभिश्च ।\nबभौ सविद्युत्स्तनयित्नुकल्पा\nजलागमे द्यौरिव जातमेघा ॥","meaning":{"en":"That army, with King Shantanu's son, great chariot-warriors, elephants and horses, looked like the sky in the rainy season, full of lightning, thunder and rising clouds."}},{"n":6,"text":"ततो रणायाभिमुखी प्रयाता\nप्रत्यर्जुनं शांतनवाभिगुप्ता ।\nसेना महोग्रा सहसा कुरूणां\nवेगो यथा भीम इवापगायाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the fierce Kuru army, guarded by Shantanu's son, advanced suddenly to meet Arjuna, fearsome in its rush like a river in flood."}},{"n":7,"text":"तं व्यालनानाविधगूढसारं\nगजाश्वपादातरथौघपक्षम् ।\nव्यूहं महामेघसमं महात्मा\nददर्श दूरात्कपिराजकेतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great-souled one whose banner bears the king of apes saw from afar that formation, like a great cloud, its strength hidden in many kinds of serpent-shaped ranks, with wings of elephants, horses, foot and chariots."}},{"n":8,"text":"स निर्ययौ केतुमता रथेन\nनरर्षभः श्वेतहयेन वीरः ।\nवरूथिना सैन्यमुखे महात्मा\nवधे धृतः सर्वसपत्नयूनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The bull among men, the white-horsed hero, came forth in his armored chariot with its banner, at the front of the army, resolved to kill all the young enemies."}},{"n":9,"text":"सूपस्करं सोत्तरबन्धुरेषं\nयत्तं यदूनामृषभेण संख्ये ।\nकपिध्वजं प्रेक्ष्य विषेदुराजौ\nसहैव पुत्रैस्तव कौरवेयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the ape-bannered chariot, well furnished, with its fine seat and pole, driven in battle by the bull of the Yadus, the Kauravas and your sons sank in spirit."}},{"n":10,"text":"प्रकर्षता गुप्तमुदायुधेन\nकिरीटिना लोकमहारथेन ।\nतं व्यूहराजं ददृशुस्त्वदीया-\nश्चतुश्चतुर्व्यालसहस्रकीर्णम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Led by Kiritin, the great chariot-warrior of the world, weapon raised, they saw that king of formations, guarded and scattered with thousands of fours of serpent-ranks."}},{"n":11,"text":"यथा हि पूर्वेऽहनि धर्मराज्ञा\nव्यूहः कृतः कौरवनन्दनेन ।\nतथा तथोद्देशमुपेत्य तस्थुः\nपाञ्चालमुख्यैः सह चेदिमुख्याः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Yudhishthira had arrayed the formation the day before, so the Kuru delight, and so the chief Chedis with the leading Panchalas, came up to their positions and stood."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततो महावेगसमाहतानि\nभेरीसहस्राणि विनेदुराजौ ।\nशङ्खस्वना दुन्दुभिनिस्वनाश्च\nसर्वेष्वनीकेषु ससिंहनादाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then thousands of bheris struck with great force sounded in the battle, with conch-blasts, dundubhi-sounds and lion-roars in all the divisions."}},{"n":13,"text":"ततः सबाणानि महास्वनानि\nविस्फार्यमाणानि धनूंषि वीरैः ।\nक्षणेन भेरीपणवप्रणादा-\nनन्तर्दधुः शङ्खमहास्वनाश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the loud bows, with their arrows, drawn wide by heroes, in a moment drowned out the din of bheris and drums and the great blare of conches."}},{"n":14,"text":"तच्छङ्खशब्दावृतमन्तरिक्ष-\nमुद्धूतभौमद्रुतरेणुजालम् ।\nमहावितानावततप्रकाश-\nमालोक्य वीराः सहसाभिपेतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the sky filled with conch-sounds, and nets of dust thrown up from the earth by the rushing troops, spread like a great canopy, the heroes suddenly charged."}},{"n":15,"text":"रथी रथेनाभिहतः ससूतः\nपपात साश्वः सरथः सकेतुः ।\nगजो गजेनाभिहतः पपात\nपदातिना चाभिहतः पदातिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chariot-warrior fell struck by chariot-warrior with his charioteer, horses, chariot and banner; elephant fell struck by elephant; foot soldier fell struck by foot soldier."}},{"n":16,"text":"आवर्तमानान्यभिवर्तमानै-\nर्बाणैः क्षतान्यद्भुतदर्शनानि ।\nप्रासैश्च खड्गैश्च समाहतानि\nसदश्ववृन्दानि सदश्ववृन्दैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wheeling squadrons, pierced by arrows from wheeling squadrons, of fine horses wondrous to see, were struck down with lances and swords."}},{"n":17,"text":"सुवर्णतारागणभूषितानि\nशरावराणि प्रहितानि वीरैः ।\nविदार्यमाणानि परश्वधैश्च\nप्रासैश्च खड्गैश्च निपेतुरुर्व्याम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shields adorned with golden stars, hurled by heroes and cut apart with axes, lances and swords, fell to the earth."}},{"n":18,"text":"गजैर्विषाणैर्वरहस्तरुग्णाः\nकेचित्ससूता रथिनः प्रपेतुः ।\nगजर्षभाश्चापि रथर्षभेण\nनिपेतिरे बाणहताः पृथिव्याम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some chariot-warriors with their charioteers fell, crushed by elephants' tusks and fine trunks; and great elephants fell to earth struck down by arrows from great chariot-warriors."}},{"n":19,"text":"गजौघवेगोद्धतसादितानां\nश्रुत्वा निषेदुर्वसुधां मनुष्याः ।\nआर्तस्वरं सादिपदातियूनां\nविषाणगात्रावरताडितानाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men crouched on the earth hearing the cries of horsemen and young foot soldiers struck down by the rush of masses of elephants, battered by tusks and bodies."}},{"n":20,"text":"संभ्रान्तनागाश्वरथे प्रसूते\nमहाभये सादिपदातियूनाम् ।\nमहारथैः संपरिवार्यमाणं\nददर्श भीष्मः कपिराजकेतुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that great fear, as elephants, horses and chariots reeled, and horsemen and young foot soldiers panicked, Bhishma saw the ape-bannered Arjuna ringed in by great chariot-warriors."}},{"n":21,"text":"तं पञ्चतालोच्छ्रिततालकेतुः\nसदश्ववेगोद्धतवीर्ययातः ।\nमहास्त्रबाणाशनिदीप्तमार्गं\nकिरीटिनं शांतनवोऽभ्यधावत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma, with his palm-tree banner five palms high and a drive swift with his fine horses' speed, rushed at Kiritin, whose path blazed with bolts of great weapons and arrows."}},{"n":22,"text":"तथैव शक्रप्रतिमानकल्प-\nमिन्द्रात्मजं द्रोणमुखाभिसस्रुः ।\nकृपश्च शल्यश्च विविंशतिश्च\nदुर्योधनः सौमदत्तिश्च राजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And so Kripa, Shalya, Vivimshati, Duryodhana and Somadatta's son, king, came with Drona at their head against Indra's son, who was like Shakra himself."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततो रथानीकमुखादुपेत्य\nसर्वास्त्रवित्काञ्चनचित्रवर्मा ।\nजवेन शूरोऽभिससार सर्वां-\nस्तथार्जुनस्यात्र सुतोऽभिमन्युः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Abhimanyu, Arjuna's son, a hero knowing all weapons, in gold-bright armor, came from the front of the chariot division and swiftly attacked them all."}},{"n":24,"text":"तेषां महास्त्राणि महारथाना-\nमसक्तकर्मा विनिहत्य कार्ष्णिः ।\nबभौ महामन्त्रहुतार्चिमाली\nसदोगतः सन्भगवानिवाग्निः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having destroyed the great weapons of those great chariot-warriors without hindrance, Krishna's grandson Abhimanyu shone like the blessed fire in the sacrificial hall, wreathed in flames fed by great mantras."}},{"n":25,"text":"ततः स तूर्णं रुधिरोदफेनां\nकृत्वा नदीं वैशसने रिपूणाम् ।\nजगाम सौभद्रमतीत्य भीष्मो\nमहारथं पार्थमदीनसत्त्वः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhishma, undaunted, quickly made a river of blood and foam in that slaughter of his foes, passed by Subhadra's son, and went to the great chariot-warrior Partha."}},{"n":26,"text":"ततः प्रहस्याद्भुतदर्शनेन\nगाण्डीवनिर्ह्रादमहास्वनेन ।\nविपाठजालेन महास्त्रजालं\nविनाशयामास किरीटमाली ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Kiritin, laughing, with the wondrous sight and the great sound of Gandiva's twang, destroyed that great net of weapons with a net of vipathas."}},{"n":27,"text":"तमुत्तमं सर्वधनुर्धराणा-\nमसक्तकर्मा कपिराजकेतुः ।\nभीष्मं महात्माभिववर्ष तूर्णं\nशरौघजालैर्विमलैश्च भल्लैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The ape-bannered Arjuna, great-souled and unhindered in his work, the best of all archers, swiftly rained showers and nets of bright arrows and broad-headed shafts on Bhishma."}},{"n":28,"text":"एवंविधं कार्मुकभीमनाद-\nमदीनवत्सत्पुरुषोत्तमाभ्याम् ।\nददर्श लोकः कुरुसृञ्जयाश्च\nतद्द्वैरथं भीष्मधनंजयाभ्याम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Such was the duel between Bhishma and Dhananjaya, those two undaunted best of men, with their bows of terrible sound, which the world and the Kurus and Srinjayas watched."}}]}]}